Step 1: Configure GitHub Environments
In your GitHub repository, navigate to Settings → Environments (in the left sidebar).

Click New environment.

Name it staging and click Configure environment.

Under Environment variables, click Add variable:

Name: ENVIRONMENT_NAME

Value: staging

Go back to Environments and click New environment.

Name it production and click Configure environment.

Under Environment protection rules, check Required reviewers.

Add your GitHub username as a reviewer.

Under Environment variables, click Add variable:

Name: ENVIRONMENT_NAME

Value: production

Step 2: Update .github/workflows/pipeline.yml
Replace your existing workflow file with the multi-environment pipeline:

name: Multi-Environment CI/CD Pipeline

on:
  push:
    branches: [ "main" ]
  pull_request:
    branches: [ "main" ]

jobs:
  # JOB 1: Continuous Integration (Unit Tests)
  unit-tests:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - name: Checkout Code
        uses: actions/checkout@v4.2.2

      - name: Set up Python
        uses: actions/setup-python@v5.4.0
        with:
          python-version: '3.11'

      - name: Install Dependencies
        run: |
          python -m pip install --upgrade pip
          pip install -r requirements.txt

      - name: Run Pytest Suite
        run: |
          python -m pytest

  # JOB 2: Deploy to Staging Environment
  deploy-staging:
    needs: unit-tests
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' && github.event_name == 'push'
    environment:
      name: staging

    steps:
      - name: Checkout Code
        uses: actions/checkout@v4.2.2

      - name: Simulate Staging Deployment
        run: |
          echo "Deploying commit ${{ github.sha }} to ${{ vars.ENVIRONMENT_NAME }}..."
          # In real-world setups, this is where Terraform, Helm, or AWS ECS commands run
          echo "Staging deployment successful!"

  # JOB 3: Staging Automated Smoke Checks
  staging-smoke-test:
    needs: deploy-staging
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' && github.event_name == 'push'

    steps:
      - name: Run Staging Smoke Tests
        run: |
          echo "Validating health probes in Staging..."
          echo "Simulated: curl http://staging.internal/health -> 200 OK"
          echo "Staging verification passed!"

  # JOB 4: Deploy to Production (Gated by Required Reviewer)
  deploy-production:
    needs: staging-smoke-test
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' && github.event_name == 'push'
    environment:
      name: production

    steps:
      - name: Checkout Code
        uses: actions/checkout@v4.2.2

      - name: Execute Production Rollout
        run: |
          echo "Deploying verified commit ${{ github.sha }} to ${{ vars.ENVIRONMENT_NAME }}..."
          echo "Production deployment live!"


Step 3: Commit and Push the Workflow
Run these commands in your local repository:

git add .github/workflows/pipeline.yml
git commit -m "Configure multi-environment pipeline with staging, smoke tests, and production gate"
git push origin main


Step 4: Verify the Manual Approval Gate

Head over to the Actions tab on GitHub and open the latest workflow run.

Watch unit-tests, deploy-staging, and staging-smoke-test complete with green checkmarks.

Observe that the pipeline pauses at deploy-production with an amber status: "Waiting for review".

Click Review deployments, select the production checkbox, and click Approve and deploy.

Watch deploy-production execute to completion!